# Shell scripts must be LF on every platform.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so a checkout produces CRLF and a script
# copied to a Linux host then fails with "#!/bin/sh\r: not found" before running
# a single line. That is what happened to cleanroom.sh on VM2: the blob in git was
# clean LF the whole time, so nothing in the repository looked wrong.
#
# Forcing eol=lf at checkout makes the working copy match the blob, so a script is
# the same bytes whether it is run here or copied to a container.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Keep this file itself LF so the rules are parsed identically everywhere.
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# The Rust sources and the Python package are indifferent, but pinning them keeps
# diffs stable when a file moves between machines.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
